  "contract": [
    "Request and header ownership use renderer-scoped native identifiers; public lifecycle retains immutable occurrence identity.",
    "Confirmed original frame/loader commits transfer response custody across renderer sessions, including detach-before-parent-commit. Replaced or removed pending navigations cannot transfer.",
    "Remote initialization enables Network; body commands retain native request ID and exact response session.",
    "Renderer retirement releases unfinished/header/recording capacity; physical worker and response reservations survive logical retirement until native reply or exact destruction.",
    "Child terminal ingress closes diagnostic admission before semantic retirement; child destruction leaves root diagnostics available.",
    "Exact missing-session body replies are unavailable outcomes. Content replacement preserves other active occurrences."
  ],
