  "referenceDifferences": [
    "Both final reference runs reject the immediate response.body read for the child document returning to its parent renderer; Flashwright waits for the confirmed commit and returns the original bytes. This is explicitly outside exact error-parity claims.",
    "At the fixture observation 250 ms after child removal, the pinned reference streaming body remains pending and has no requestfailed event; page closure rejects it. Flashwright rejects at original renderer retirement, emits requestfailed, and retains a usable parent. This is a lifecycle observation, not a performance metric."
  ],
